# EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR: (21,3): Undefined function/method call: 'Keep(..)'
# EXPECT_ERROR_COUNT: 2
#~
An array is not boxed, and one value is not an array of holders. Neither call
fits its function, and each is reported once, as the call it is: no holder
constructor is tried on the array ('IntRef->New(Int[])' was reported for line
21), and the Int is not passed as the IntRef[] (line 22 compiled, and the
program failed the load-time verifier: "an object used as an array").
~#
class BadBoxingArrayForHolder {
	function : Keep(value : IntRef) ~ Int {
		return value->Get();
	}

	function : KeepAll(values : IntRef[]) ~ Int {
		return values->Size();
	}

	function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
		values := Int->New[3];
		Keep(values)->PrintLine();
		KeepAll(5)->PrintLine();
	}
}
